Scope of this license
---------------------

Everything in this repository is Apache-2.0. Per ADR-13 the grant boundary is
drawn at the **repository**, not file by file, so no directory here is carved
out and nothing here needs a per-file licence header to be covered.

Until 2026-09-16 this file also listed components that were *excluded* from the
grant, because Gurdy was planned as an open core with a paid fleet tier. **That
plan was abandoned and there are no excluded components.** Gurdy is entirely
open source. Nothing is withheld, nothing is distributed from a second
repository, and no capability is reserved for a paid build.

The list below is therefore descriptive rather than a boundary — it is what is
here, not what is permitted:

  - gurdy-proxy       interceptor proxy and the monitor actuator; the
                      local single-instance enforce actuator when it ships
                      (Phase 2 — it is not implemented today)
  - gurdy-verify      offline ledger verifier
  - the Transaction Identity Service, policy host, and decision ledger
  - the starter policy set, and the adversarial corpus that gates it
  - the Gurdy SDKs (Python, TypeScript) and the shared conformance suite
  - gurdy-report, the local report (BR-11)

Two things the old text named as paid, for anyone who read this file before:
fleet coordination (central ledger, fleet policy distribution, fleet-wide
rollout and rollback, central attestation) and the framework-mapped evidence
report that maps decisions to NIST AI RMF / ISO 42001 / EU AI Act controls.
Neither is withheld. Both are simply **unbuilt**, tracked in docs/roadmap.md,
and will be Apache-2.0 here when they exist.
